    },
    {
      "id": "bde1d4fe71d5",
      "source": " Constant",
      "target": " Constant（常量）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "0079746f7a64",
      "source": "Generates a signal with values that don’t change over time.",
      "target": "生成一个数值不会随时间变化的信号。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "a6f3d73a78bb",
      "source": "This can be useful for when you want to control multiple parameters with the same slider.",
      "target": "当你想用同一个滑块控制多个参数时，这会很有用。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "99d75d956d20",
      "source": "This modulator is unique as it has the ",
      "target": "此调制器比较特殊，因为它具有 ",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "f8605ea969cc",
      "source": "Mode",
      "target": "Mode",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "08e6cafe08c8",
      "source": " dropdown parameter to select the most suitable type of control.",
      "target": " 下拉参数，可用于选择最合适的控制类型。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "a615900a333d",
      "source": " Oscillator",
      "target": " Oscillator（振荡器）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "3b38df5b70a9",
      "source": "Generates a signal where the values change over a specified waveform.",
      "target": "生成一个数值会沿指定波形变化的信号。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "8d075846a8ef",
      "source": "This can be useful to add some turbulence into your project by having parameters deviate from their base value in a ,for example, random way.",
      "target": "这可用于向项目中添加一些扰动，例如让参数以随机方式偏离其基础值。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "db09467da849",
      "source": " Cycle",
      "target": " Cycle（循环）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "11f93054c61a",
      "source": "A version of the saw waveform. Repeats a linear value change from ",
      "target": "锯齿波形的一种版本。会重复执行从 ",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "47b20f4e0fef",
      "source": " to ",
      "target": " 到 ",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "8b3dec38ae5d",
      "source": "This is used to get something continuously rotating.",
      "target": "这用于让某些内容持续旋转。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "0be418c6e2e5",
      "source": " Combine",
      "target": " Combine（组合）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "9ce784226154",
      "source": "This node doesn’t generate a signal, but combines multiple signals in a specified mathematical way.",
      "target": "此节点不会生成信号，而是以指定的数学方式组合多个信号。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "e4ca4ec7f5e2",
      "source": " Math",
      "target": " Math（数学）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "de5afb8d5d9e",
      "source": "This node has a text field where you can write you own math expressions to generate a signal.",
      "target": "此节点有一个文本字段，你可以在其中编写自己的数学表达式来生成信号。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "4f90ab509c4d",
      "source": " Time Shift",
      "target": " Time Shift（时间偏移）",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "3cdc4dc63e0f",
      "source": "Doesn’t generate a signal, but does a temporal offset on the incoming signal.",
      "target": "不会生成信号，而是对传入信号进行时间偏移。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "64001e212f3f",
      "source": " ADSR",
      "target": " ADSR",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "5688c651dbfc",
      "source": "The ADSR Node allows you to map a specific parameter to an ADSR Envelope.",
      "target": "ADSR 节点允许将特定参数映射到 ADSR 包络。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "6fa1ebb23cad",
      "source": "ADSR stands for Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release. Once the ADSR node ",
      "target": "ADSR 代表 Attack（起音）、Decay（衰减）、Sustain（延音）、Release（释音）。ADSR 节点的 ",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "3fd4bab0d7db",
      "source": "Active",
      "target": "Active",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "9e15b4478982",
      "source": " checkbox is on, the envelope will be engaged, starting with the ‘attack’. Attack is the amount of time it takes for the base value of the assigned parameter to reach its peak value, dictated by the Amount %. Decay is the duration of time it takes to get from the peak value to the Sustain value. Sustain is the percentage inbetween the Base and Amount value, and this value will remain the same until the ADSR node is innactive. Once the Active binary is turned off, you will ‘release’ the envelope. Release is the time it takes for the Sustain value to return to the Base value.",
      "target": " 复选框开启后，包络会被触发，并从 attack（起音）开始。Attack（起音）是指定参数的基础值到达峰值所需的时间，峰值由 Amount % 决定。Decay（衰减）是从峰值到 Sustain（延音）值所需的时间。Sustain（延音）是 Base 与 Amount 值之间的百分比；该值会保持不变，直到 ADSR 节点变为非活动状态。Active 二值开关关闭后，包络会进入 release（释音）。Release（释音）是 Sustain（延音）值返回 Base 值所需的时间。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fc83276ded07",
      "source": "This node is especcially useful in combination with the MIDI node.",
      "target": "此节点与 MIDI 节点结合使用时尤其有用。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "502669b787a8",
      "source": " MIDI",
      "target": " MIDI",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "c70ab20fd208",
      "source": "Generates a signal based on pressing buttons on a MIDI controller like a keyboard.",
      "target": "根据键盘等 MIDI 控制器上的按键操作生成信号。",
      "note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "a7df66022b23",
      "source": "To use this you first need to check ",
